==Galician==
[[File:Peña Trevinca ao fondo.JPG |thumb|Pena Trevinca, with 2127m, is the highest mountain in Galicia]]
===Etymology===
From Old Galician and {{inh|gl|roa-opt|montanna}} (13th century, {{w|Cantigas de Santa Maria}}), from {{inh|gl|VL.|*montania|*montānia, montānea}}, feminine of {{m|la||*montānius, montāneus|mountainous}}, alteration of {{inh|gl|la|montānus}}, from {{m|la|mōns||mountain}}, from {{der|gl|ine-pro|*men-}}. Cognate with {{cog|pt|montanha}} and {{cog|es|montaña}}. 

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/monˈtaɲa̝/|lang=gl}}

===Noun===
{{gl-noun|f}}

# [[mountain]]
# [[highlands]]
#* '''1853''', J. M. Pintos, ''A Gaita Gallega'', page 58:
#*: ''Alá de donde vimos na '''montaña''' a miseria é tan grande que non pode a xente se queixar ''
#*:: There, where we came from, in the '''highlands''', misery is so large that people can't even complain

